---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Clock from '../components/Clock.astro';
import Dial from '../components/Dial.astro';
import snapshot from '../data/calendar.json';
import { CALENDAR_URL, formatDate, getLedgerGroups, getReleaseState, releaseInterval, releaseLine, releaseTiming } from '../lib/releases';
const { latest, target, lts, ltsPatch } = getReleaseState(snapshot);
const ledgerGroups = getLedgerGroups(snapshot, 'recent');
---
<Layout>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow intro-eyebrow"><img src="/images/duckdb.svg" alt="" width="22" height="22" /> DuckDB release watch</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">Keeping time<br />with <em>DuckDB.</em></h1>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-note">
        <span class="small-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p>Release dates and support deadlines.<br />Updated from DuckDB’s official calendar.</p>
        <div class="live-time"><span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><time id="wall-clock">UTC</time><span class="live-label">Right now</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="release-board" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="board-screw screw-tl" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="board-screw screw-tr" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="board-screw screw-bl" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="board-screw screw-br" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="board-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow board-eyebrow" id="target-eyebrow">Next major release</p>
          <h2 id="next-title">DuckDB <span class="version-number">2.0</span><span class="codename">“Cyanoptera”</span></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="board-mode"><span id="target-badge" class="status-badge"><span></span> On the way</span><button id="focus-toggle" class="icon-button" aria-label="Enter focus mode" aria-pressed="false" title="Focus mode"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 3H3v4m10-4h4v4M3 13v4h4m10-4v4h-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" /></svg></button></div>
      </div>
      <Clock id="release-clock" large />
      <p id="target-message" class="target-message" hidden></p>
      <div class="board-footer">
        <p><span class="calendar-icon" aria-hidden="true">▦</span><span id="target-date">{target ? formatDate(target.date, 'long') : 'Date to be announced'}</span><span class="tentative" id="tentative-label">Tentative</span></p>
        <a id="calendar-download" class="board-link" href="/duckdb-2.0.ics" download>Add to calendar <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="board-caption"><span><span class="tiny-cross" aria-hidden="true">＋</span> Good software is worth the wait.</span><a href="#about-the-clock">Date-based countdown · UTC <span aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span></a></div>

    <section class="secondary-clocks" aria-label="Release and support clocks">
      <article class="clock-card latest-card">
        <div class="card-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">Latest release</p><h2>Time since last release.</h2></div>
          <Dial />
        </div>
        <div class="release-meta"><span class="release-pill" id="latest-version">v{latest?.version ?? '—'}</span><span id="latest-codename">{latest?.codename || 'Patch release'}</span><span class="meta-trailing">and counting</span></div>
        <Clock id="latest-clock" />
        <div class="card-footer"><span>Released <time id="latest-date" datetime={latest?.date}>{latest ? formatDate(latest.date) : '—'}</time></span><a id="latest-link" href={latest?.url ?? CALENDAR_URL}>Release notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="clock-card lts-card">
        <div class="card-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">LTS community support</p><h2 id="lts-title">LTS support remaining.</h2></div>
          <Dial kind="support" />
        </div>
        <div class="release-meta"><span class="release-pill" id="lts-version">v{lts ? releaseLine(lts.version) : '—'} LTS</span><span id="lts-codename">{lts?.codename}</span><span id="lts-status" class="meta-trailing">Remaining</span></div>
        <Clock id="lts-clock" />
        <div class="support-meter" role="meter" aria-label="LTS support window remaining" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="0" id="support-meter"><div id="support-fill"></div></div>
        <div class="card-footer"><span>Support ends <time id="lts-end" datetime={lts?.endOfLife ?? undefined}>{lts?.endOfLife ? formatDate(lts.endOfLife) : '—'}</time></span><a href={`${CALENDAR_URL}#lts-releases`}>Support policy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section id="release-ledger" class="ledger-section" aria-labelledby="ledger-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="ledger-title">Release ledger<span class="heading-period">.</span></h2><a class="text-link" href={CALENDAR_URL}>View on duckdb.org <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="release-ledger">
        <div class="ledger-heading"><p id="ledger-description">The latest two release lines, with every patch.</p><div class="filter-controls" role="group" aria-label="Filter releases"><button data-filter="recent" aria-pressed="true">Recent</button><button data-filter="upcoming" aria-pressed="false">Upcoming</button><button data-filter="lts" aria-pressed="false">LTS</button></div></div>
        <div class="table-scroll"><table id="release-table">
          <caption class="sr-only">DuckDB releases from the official calendar</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Release</th><th scope="col">Date <span class="th-note">/ UTC</span></th><th scope="col" class="age-heading" id="release-age-heading">Age</th><th scope="col" class="interval-heading">Interval</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Details</span></th></tr></thead>
          {ledgerGroups.map((group) => <tbody class="release-group" data-release-line={group.line}>
            <tr class="release-group-heading"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="6"><div class="branch-heading"><strong>DuckDB {group.line}</strong>{group.codename && <span class="branch-codename">{group.codename}</span>}{group.lts && <span class="branch-lts">LTS</span>}<span class="branch-count">{group.releases.length} {group.releases.length === 1 ? 'release' : 'releases'}</span></div></th></tr>
            {group.releases.map((r) => {
              const timing = releaseTiming(r.date, false);
              const interval = releaseInterval(r, snapshot, false);
              return <tr class="release-row"><th scope="row"><span class="release-product">DuckDB </span><span>{r.version}</span></th><td><time datetime={r.date}>{formatDate(r.date)}</time></td><td class="release-age" data-release-date={r.date} data-planned="false" title={timing.label} aria-label={timing.label}>{timing.text}</td><td class="release-interval" title={interval.label} aria-label={interval.label}>{interval.text}</td><td><span class="table-status">Released</span></td><td><a href={r.url} aria-label={`DuckDB ${r.version} release notes`}>↗</a></td></tr>;
            })}
          </tbody>)}
        </table></div>
        <p class="ledger-note">Intervals compare versions within the same branch. Planned dates and intervals (~) may change.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="about-the-clock" class="about-section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="about-heading"><img src="/images/duckdb.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /><h2 id="about-title">A note on the clocks.</h2></div>
      <div class="about-copy"><p>All dates come from the <a href={CALENDAR_URL}>DuckDB release calendar</a>. Release dates are tentative; the DuckDB team may take a little longer to get things right.</p><details><summary>How we keep time <span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="methodology"><p>The calendar publishes dates, not launch times. Every clock uses <strong>00:00 UTC</strong> on the listed date as a consistent reference, not a promised release time. At zero, a planned release switches to “Release day” or “Awaiting release” until the calendar confirms it.</p><p>The last-release clock includes patch releases and uses the most recent published date across all release lines. The LTS clock uses the calendar’s explicit end-of-life date for the latest LTS line, not an assumed one-year anniversary. <span id="lts-patch-note">The latest LTS patch is v{ltsPatch?.version}.</span></p><p>The source is checked when you open the page and every hour, with an hourly cache on Cloudflare. If the source cannot be reached, the clocks keep running from the last available snapshot and show its age. Calendar downloads are one-time, all-day reminders; they do not update automatically.</p></div></details></div>
    </section>
    <div class="source-status"><p><span class="source-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span id="source-label">Calendar snapshot</span><span class="source-separator">/</span><span id="source-checked">Checked {formatDate(snapshot.fetchedAt.slice(0, 10))}</span></p><button id="refresh-source">Refresh source <span aria-hidden="true">↻</span></button></div>
    <noscript><p class="noscript-note">Enable JavaScript for ticking clocks and release filters. The release dates above remain available. <a href={CALENDAR_URL}>View the full DuckDB calendar.</a></p></noscript>
  </main>
  <script id="calendar-data" type="application/json" set:html={JSON.stringify(snapshot).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c')} />
  <script>
    import '../scripts/clock.ts';
  </script>
</Layout>
